exists su name brief video script source thrust intent ob text quoted.text.The generator is asked to write a short spoken script that combines transcript-grounded historical facts with present-day parallels and a call to action. Treat present-day parallels as commentary by default. Only fail for historical grounding when the script adds or distorts concrete historical facts (people, events, laws, mechanisms) beyond the transcript..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name brief video script fact one prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing spoken script lines for a 30-60 second history short.

Task:
- Write 2-3 short spoken sentences.
- Use one shocking historical fact from the transcript.
- Tie it to a clear modern parallel.
- Keep this segment between 20 and 34 words.

Rules:
- Dramatic, authoritative tone.
- Historical claims must come only from the provided transcript.
- Do not introduce new people, places, events, or policies not present in the transcript.
- Plain prose only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no quotes around the full output.
.text.quoted be text ya

exists su name brief video script fact two prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing the next spoken segment for the same short.

Task:
- Write 2-3 short spoken sentences.
- Use a different shocking historical fact than the one already used.
- Tie it to a clear modern parallel.
- Keep this segment between 20 and 34 words.

Rules:
- Do not repeat the same person/event/core claim from the prior segment.
- Dramatic, authoritative tone.
- Historical claims must come only from the provided transcript.
- Do not introduce new people, places, events, or policies not present in the transcript.
- Plain prose only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no quotes around the full output.
.text.quoted be text ya

